title: '[FRAME] Add `AccountLike` trait and `#[pallet::as_account]` for custom origin account tracking'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Custom pallet origins can now expose an account and opt in to nonce tracking and fee payment,
    which until now only worked for `frame_system::RawOrigin::Signed`.

    - `#[pallet::as_account(<closure>)]` on an origin enum variant maps the variant to an account.
    - `#[pallet::nonce_provider]` and `#[pallet::fee_payer]` on the same variant make `CheckNonce`
      and `ChargeTransactionPayment` (and the `ChargeAssetTxPayment` extensions) use that account.
      Each is optional; a variant using only one of them must provide the other protection itself.
    - `frame_system::ensure_account` extends `ensure_signed` to accept any origin which exposes an
      account. `pallet-collective` exposes the account of its `Member` origin.

    This is backed by the new `frame_support::traits::AccountLike` trait. Nonce checking and fee
    payment are unchanged for existing origins.

    Breaking changes:
    - A type alias origin (`#[pallet::origin] pub type Origin<..> = SomeType<..>;`) now requires
      the aliased type to implement `AccountLike<AccountId>`. An empty `impl` keeps the previous
      behaviour.
    - `CallerTrait<AccountId>` now has `AccountLike<AccountId>` as a supertrait, so manual
      implementations of `CallerTrait` must implement it too.
crates:
- name: frame-support
  bump: major
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: major
- name: frame-system
  bump: minor
- name: frame-system-benchmarking
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-transaction-payment
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-asset-tx-payment
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-asset-conversion-tx-payment
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-collective
  bump: minor
